def main():
 p=HERE/'report/REPORT.md';text=p.read_text().split('\n## Post-run source and reproducibility audit')[0];audit=read(HERE/'report/source-audit.json');m=read(HERE/'manifest.json')
 old='Sizes: 10, 50, 100, 250, 1,000 and 6,006. The union retains the supplied PDF grid and the newer repository grid supplied by the parent reviewer. The repository project_proposal.tex/reference_metrics.py were not found locally; direct inspection here used the supplied PDF and research-plan contract. Source hashes and the exact seed/library algorithm are in protocol.json, manifest.json and independent-audit.json.'
 new='The requested four-size subset is 50, 250, 1,000 and 6,006: 20 queries × 4 sizes = 80 libraries. Two additional frozen sizes, 10 and 100, preserve the supplied PDF grid, giving 20 × 6 = 120 libraries total. The repository proposal at commit041f2ce specifies50/250/1000; the user requested seed5150 and the full6006 endpoint. The same20 query IDs and exact per-query library are used across all17 retrieval methods. The expensive selector and reranker panels use the same first2 query IDs, not20.\n\nAt execution time, direct source inspection used the supplied PDF and research-plan contract, plus the parent reviewer’s repository findings. After execution, project_proposal.tex and skillret-pilot/reference_metrics.py were fetched through the connected GitHub app and read at041f2ce. The comparison below is a local adaptation, not exact reproduction of the repository proposal. The post-run audit documents every material difference without altering any completed run.'
 text=text.replace(old,new)
 lines=['','## Post-run source and reproducibility audit','', 'Sources read after execution: [project_proposal.tex](https://github.com/speccy88/mia5150/blob/041f2ce/project_proposal.tex) and [reference_metrics.py](https://github.com/speccy88/mia5150/blob/041f2ce/skillret-pilot/reference_metrics.py). The reviewed pure-standard-library helper was used only for an offline audit, never model inference. All120 memberships exactly match its sampler at seed5150. All18,360 checked retrieval scalar values match its definitions for Recall/Precision/NDCG/Completeness at5/10 and MRR at5.','', 'Display order differs in all120 cases: the helper hashes seed NUL query_id NUL display NUL skill_id; the frozen local protocol hashes seed NUL display NUL query_id NUL skill_id. Both are label-independent and shared across methods, but are not byte-identical to the source helper. Completed predictions and frozen libraries were not rewritten.','', 'Other material deviations from the original proposal:','', '- The exact BGE-small-en-v1.5 vector arm is untested here. The exact BGE-backed native domain-vector arm is also untested. Tested local domain variants use the same local selector to predict six major categories and restrict SkillRet-0.6B vectors; no global fallback. The centroid arm is a separate ablation and is not equivalent to an LM router.','- Common local metadata is original name + separator + description, capped once at1,024 characters. The proposal’s additional128-BGE-token cap is not applied. Neural encoder caps are listed below. Thus these results cannot be compared numerically to the historical BGE metadata baseline as a method-only change.','- Direct localhost llama.cpp generation and opaque aliases replace native LangChain Deep Agents SkillsMiddleware/StateBackend and select_skills calls returning original IDs. That middleware integration and the separate native activation-read check are not reproduced in this experiment. No skill bodies are executed.','- Local Qwen selectors replace the proposal’s hosted DeepSeek/provider configuration. Paid services are outside this experiment. Seed5150 replaces42. The20 queries are selected deterministically from an existing exposed128-query cache panel; the proposal’s previously unused20-query/4192-ID-final-test claim does not apply because all4392 public queries have prior exposure.','- Only2 queries receive generation/reranking. This is an explicit resource-bounded diagnostic, not a20-query selection comparison.','', '### Complete list of17 retrieval identities','', '| Identity | Definition |','|---|---|','| bm25 | Common capped metadata; library-local IDF; top100 retained |','| qwen_embed_06 | Qwen3-Embedding-0.6B native query/document embeddings |','| skillret_embed_06 | SKILLRET-Embedding-0.6B native embeddings |','| skillrouter_embed_06 | SkillRouter-Embedding-0.6B native embeddings |','| skillreason_embed_06 | SkillReason-embedding-0.6b native embeddings |','| eg2_text270m_fp32 | EmbeddingGemma2 text-only271M parameters, native SearchQuery/Document prompts |','| jina_nano239m_fp32 | Jina v5 text nano239M, native retrieval adapter and query/document prompts |','| hybrid_rrf60 | Equal RRF60 of BM25 and SkillRet top100 |','| domain_centroid | Mean SkillRet similarity per major category; choose one, then restrict dense order; no LM |','| field_tfidf | Equal name/description TF-IDF cosine, library-local IDF |','| mmr5 | Fixed lambda0.8, SkillRet top20, five-item budget and frozen relevance gate |','| dsr5 | Fixed0.9 relevance/diversity logdet blend on SkillRet top20; five-item budget |','| dense20 | SkillRet top20 candidate control |','| dense30 | SkillRet top30 candidate control |','| roundrobin20 | Deduplicated alternating BM25/SkillRet candidates, budget20 |','| dense20_novel10 | Preserve SkillRet top20, append up to10 novel BM25 candidates; budget30 |','| query_clause_bm25 | Whole query plus first3 qualifying deterministic clauses, equal RRF60; no LM rewriting |','', 'Exact ties use original skill-ID ordering for retrieval/fusion; pointwise reranker ties use frozen pool order. Candidate-budget controls are paired at equal budgets. All known gold skills are included only by library construction, not by ranking, prompting or final selection.','', '### Query panel and configuration','', 'Query IDs: '+', '.join(q['id'] for q in m['queries'])+'.','', 'Gold multiplicities:10 single-positive,8 double-positive,2 triple-positive queries. Both expensive panels use q-03666 (one positive) and q-00674 (three positives). Generative sizes are all6; reranker sizes are50/1000/6006 with the same SkillRet top20 pools across models.','', '| Role | Deployment | Input/context control |','|---|---|','| Four0.6B encoders | FP16, normalized1024-dimensional vectors | Native prompts; max1024 tokens; batch1 for refreshed headers |','| EG2 text encoder | FP32, eager attention,271,002,624 loaded text parameters;768-dimensional vectors | Native SearchQuery/Document; max512 tokens; batch1 |','| Jina nano encoder | FP32, eager attention,238,897,920 parameters;768-dimensional vectors | Native retrieval adapter; max1024 tokens; batch1 |','| Small selector/router | Qwen3-0.6B Q8_0 |8192 context;256 output tokens; temperature0; seed5150; thinking disabled |','| Medium selector/router | Qwen3.5-4B Q4_K_M |Same8192/256/temperature0/seed5150 controls |','| Small reranker | SKILLRET-Reranker-0.6B FP16 local conversion |2048 context; native yes-minus-no logits; batch1; no truncation |','| Medium reranker | JevK5-4B-v0.3 Q5_K_M |2048 context; native four-option Score; temperature1.22; top256 logprobs; missing options invalidate |','|8B fit/rerank challenger | Qwen3-Reranker-8B Q4_K_M |2048 context; one generated token; temperature0; native yes/no top256 readout; stopped after failure |','', 'llama.cpp is cached build b11425/CUDA12.8, offline, localhost-only, all GPU layers, t=1/tb=1, batch128/microbatch128, dio loading, cache RAM0 and context checkpoints0. Embedding compute threads are1; auxiliary runtime threads may be present. One GPU workload runs at a time.','', '### Pinned artifacts','', 'Frozen protocol SHA-256: `'+audit['protocol_sha256']+'`.','', 'Library SHA-256: `'+audit['library_sha256']+'`.','', 'Rendered text SHA-256: `'+audit['text_sha256']+'`.','', 'Dataset revision: `6583d7d2ed07644d0fb8938ed8178f3a7dc42a12`. Official scorer source revision: `0cc508e6bfcfff1fe6352d90ff5957ba38a64bba`.','', '| Dataset file | SHA-256 |','|---|---|']
 for name,h in audit['source_data_sha256'].items():lines.append(f'| {name} | `{h}` |')
 lines+=['','| Encoder repository | Revision | Weight SHA-256 |','|---|---|---|']
 for model in audit['models']:lines.append(f"| {model['repository']} | `{model['revision']}` | `{model['weight_sha256']}` |")
 lines+=['','Other deployment pins:','', '- Qwen3-0.6B-Q8_0.gguf: `9465e63a22add5354d9bb4b99e90117043c7124007664907259bd16d043bb031`; cached repository revision `23749fefcc72300e3a2ad315e1317431b06b590a`.','- Qwen3.5-4B-Q4_K_M.gguf: `00fe7986ff5f6b463e62455821146049db6f9313603938a70800d1fb69ef11a4`; cached unsloth revision `e87f176479d0855a907a41277aca2f8ee7a09523`.','- JevK5-4B-v0.3-Q5_K_M.gguf: `b1df9869dd14c0f5b243fa956dd985f0141c3d23ec4847da4c503c73c1050601`; alibiserikbay/JevK5-GGUF revision `ec67b0bfce5119a8b11a2cdb430bb43e3fa3e82a`.','- Qwen3-Reranker-8B.Q4_K_M.gguf: `b683a127768786c0ccd87859b21a2c061ea70f30a7d14efd4476683854eea197`; mradermacher/Qwen3-Reranker-8B-GGUF revision `179cfd14a6fa8ac85a8fc9520f982dbef57ef188`. Internal tensor extents match the complete5,026,265,760-byte file; no independently verified publisher LFS checksum is available.','- Small reranker source: ThakiCloud/SKILLRET-Reranker-0.6B revision `ce09c883af78affc72a85014e040f3d28a5b1711`. Exact tensor-at-a-time FP16 cast; original unchanged. Local sharded conversion manifest SHA-256: `0ebb8d138969d9ad6ac6eac234753b5307e531cb76f72db9cb8f2957f1fcaaca`. Per-shard hashes are in that manifest.','', '### Actual new embedding work','', '| Model/stage | New documents | New queries | Document-forward seconds | Startup seconds |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
 for x in audit['embedding_work']:lines.append(f"| {x['role']} / {x['stage']} | {x['new_docs']} | {x['new_queries']} | {x['document_seconds']:.3f} | {x['startup_seconds']:.3f} |")
 lines+=['', f"Total: **{audit['total_new_document_forwards']:,} new document forwards + {audit['total_new_query_forwards']} new query forwards +8 warmups =11,568 embedding forwards**. New document-forward time is{sum(x['document_seconds'] for x in audit['embedding_work']):.3f} seconds; known new query-forward time is{sum(x.get('query_seconds_known',0) for x in audit['embedding_work']):.3f} seconds. These totals exclude historical cache creation, startup, warmup and I/O.", '', 'Each full EG2/Jina index reused299 document vectors (including30 created in its new canary) and4 query vectors. Each0.6B index reused5993 document and20 query vectors, freshly re-encoding13 headers changed by the common character cap. All new embedding inputs reported zero truncation. Historical cached timings are retained separately, never treated as fresh or free.','', 'Full-index sampled telemetry: EG2 minimum host/guest free4.24/3.52GiB, GPU free6750MiB, maximum59C; Jina minimum host/guest free3.63/3.84GiB, GPU free6880MiB, maximum59C. Neither index triggered the guard. Resource traces and model manifests, not weight size alone, support fit statements.','', '###8B failure, preservation and recovery boundary','', 'The8B scorer made3 forwards: synthetic warmup, one successful benchmark candidate, then a failure on the next candidate in q-03666/random/50. The first complete ranking is invalid; all5 later cases are unattempted. The guard did not fire and no OOM was recorded. The exact failure message/raw response was not saved before the ValueError, which is an instrumentation gap.','', 'A missing native yes/no token in the returned top256 is the likely cause, inferred from the adapter’s failure branches, the forward count and the matching small-model prompt length of331 tokens for that candidate. This is not conclusively verified against the omitted8B raw response. It is not evidence that8B cannot fit: measured free GPU memory stayed at least3120MiB and host free RAM at least2.86GiB.','', 'Recovery would require a separately versioned adapter that persists each raw response before validation and checks a reliable targeted yes/no-logit path on non-benchmark canaries before another frozen comparison. No probability-floor substitution, silent scoring change or retry of the failed request occurred in this run. All original failures remain preserved.','', '### Validation, uncertainty and release','', 'Eleven unit tests passed. The independent audit verified all120 libraries and official hand-metric cases. The additional source audit matched120 reference memberships and18,360 metric scalars. Two notebook code cells executed successfully over183 metric cells. The SVG passed XML/data-structure checks; no browser visual review is claimed.','', 'At6006, hybrid-minus-BM25 Recall@5 is+0.175 with a descriptive paired-bootstrap95% interval[0.050,0.350] (2000 resamples, seed5150;4 wins/16 ties/0 losses). Its NDCG@10 delta is+0.10845, interval[0.03761,0.19566]. These are not multiplicity-adjusted or independent-final-test confidence claims.','', 'No new paid calls, model downloads, training, external publication or Git push. Model processes and the task telemetry monitor were stopped. Final observed GPU state:0MiB used,8006MiB free,47C. SearchJev training remains queued and was not started during this audit.','']
 rendered=text+'\n'.join(lines)
 rendered=rendered.replace('| Role | Deployment | Input/context control |\n|---|---|','| Role | Deployment | Input/context control |\n|---|---|---|').replace('###8B','### 8B')
 p.write_text(rendered);print(json.dumps({'report_bytes':p.stat().st_size,'source_review_added':True,'inference_calls':0}))
